	(text "PS/2 KEYBOARD: PAK-VI DECODER, PIC16F84 SERIAL TO PARALLEL, CDP1852 INPUT PORT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "71fad942-ded1-5376-8cbf-54095f57ce42"))
	(text "The PAK-VI turns PS/2 key codes into ASCII on a serial line; the PIC (its code: pic-ps2-firmware/) puts each byte on\nRB0-7 and strobes the CDP1852's CLK. SR (character waiting) lights LED2 and, with SV1 on 2-3, drives the bus -EF\n(CPU JP1: EF3). INP on the keyboard port: CS1 = the port, CS2 = -MRD high; the 1852 drives the data bus." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "483f6dd2-c2c8-58be-9f59-018c0d2c7a8a"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
